    {
        "id": "lp_comment",
        "type": "comment",
        "name": "Long press: your own actions, one output each (echo only)",
        "info": "Hold the button and count the blinks on the 'LED' Debug node:\n- 1 blink (5 s): quiet\n- 2 blinks (10 s): reboot\n- 3 blinks (15 s): shutdown\n- 4 blinks (20 s): cancel - release safely\n\nThe action runs when you **release** the button, on its own output - no Switch node needed.\nOpen the button-morse node to rename, add or remove steps (Long press list).\n\nFor safety the Exec nodes only **echo** what they would do. When you are ready, change the commands to e.g.\n`sudo shutdown -r now` (reboot) and `sudo shutdown -h now` (shutdown).\n\nReplace the Inject nodes with a GPIO input node, and the 'LED' Debug node with a GPIO output node, on a Raspberry Pi.",
        "x": 320,
        "y": 40,
        "wires": []
    },
